id: pm-rl-proposal-revision
title: Audit revision fencing for recipe proposal publication
description: "Scope: forward-only durableRecipeProposals inference publication in meta.ts. An intent is created before awaiting proposal work, then completed by direct SDK update without an expected native revision. Reproduce peer replacement during inference and interrupted publication using a loopback model fixture and a real non-git SDK tracker. Non-goals: process executor settlement and resource refunds are separate paths, already tracked by the process recovery corrections in PR 119; this task does not assert that inference owns those paths."
type: Task
status: open
priority: 2
tags[3]: concurrency,follow-up,static-audit
created_at: "2026-10-29T17:12:16.873Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-30T13:59:08.104Z"
author: codex-agent
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: "A real SDK loopback interleaving reproduces peer replacement during inference and interruption after inference before receipt publication; success, failure, cancellation and retry preserve peer state and stored binding; retry validates every native target revision and avoids duplicate inference; process reservation and settled resource charges remain unchanged by this forward-only publication path; newly produced and released legacy receipts remain readable"
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-30T13:59:05.806Z",codex-agent,"Round-5 review clarification: the earlier description said this path has no executor failure settlement or resource refund path, rather than saying it lacks implementations of those mechanisms. The review inferred a missing refund responsibility incorrectly. Scope and non-goals are now explicit, and acceptance names the actual pre/post-inference publication failure, cancellation and retry paths, including preservation of existing process charges. No inference implementation was changed."
